  "summary": "@leejungkiin/awkit ships a dependency-manager script that fetches and executes a remote install script from a third-party GitHub repository",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js uses execSync to run `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh` and pipes the fetched content into a shell, fetching code from a mutable `master` branch under a different GitHub organization (rtk-ai/rtk) than the package publisher. The same script also contacts https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, reads os.homedir() and process.platform, and touches the local filesystem via fs.readFileSync/fs.existsSync. Because the fetch target is unpinned (branch tip rather than a commit hash or signed release), any change to that upstream repository is executed on the installer's machine. Additional bundled files (bin/awk.js, scripts/model-manager.js) combine child_process, https, POST/GET, and curl invocations in patterns consistent with runtime network fetch-and-execute. The package name and scope do not match the third-party rtk-ai organization whose install script is being executed.",
